    },
    "body": "A finite shared Context update previously damaged successful native trajectories. This adds opt-in constrained learning that accumulates one coordinated update across six shared Context bases while preserving exact native decisions throughout the eight successful trajectories. Ordinary serving keeps capture off.\n\nThe constructor visits all 17,472 scalar coordinates once in a fixed gradient order, using exact native factor rounding and deterministic ties. Independent candidate export/reload must reproduce the protected decisions and predicted score digest. All other master families and the categorical map stay fixed. This is a greedy feasible-prefix construction, not a global solver or exact recurrent derivative.\n\nThe one executed construction accepts 2,687 coordinates. Combined native CE improves 9.08399492844048 → 8.971047852627056, with successful-trajectory CE unchanged. All eight complete replies are retained, but complete replies remain **8/512**, with no newly correct failed entry. Preserve the original accepted model; the candidate is bounded optimization evidence, not a capability promotion. Saved full-pool diagnostics show the 504 failed entry targets require Generate and remain incorrect; sequential shared Generate-factor coadaptation is the recorded NOT_RUN successor, not another Context dose or seed.\n\nValidation at executed source `7f474caa819612c8f3fa6aafba2b0b2902368a26`: formatting, 13 integer Context tests, 39 fitter tests and CUDA release build pass. Actual CUDA fitting and native own-prefix evaluation completed once. Independent endpoint, actual Rust complete-file BLAKE3, prior-candidate comparison and pooled-margin audits pass. The initial compile type mismatch and the first reader's incorrect nonempty-admission requirement are retained as repaired execution defects; neither caused a model rerun. The final source changes only the report scope label and audited current-state documentation; exact final-head checks are recorded separately before queueing.\n\nFull evidence is retained in private HF `caseyallard/uor-r4-store`, revision `a98a8ec34c6a923a040fe7ce5665b1eb314b7d58`, prefix `codex/astra-context/context-0001-7f474caa81`. Both archive and manifest passed fresh-download SHA256 verification. Runtime/source/executable preservation and exact identities are recorded in current-state. No held-out chat, transfer, geometric advantage or energy claim follows.\n\nReferences #820.\n",
